        "body": "Valuation is where the inspection data earns its second return. Once condition is captured as structured points across the fleet rather than as free text, a car's price can be estimated from its attributes and its verified condition instead of from a seller's opinion, and Dooz uses AI for that valuation step.\n\nArchitecturally, valuation belongs behind the API, not in the clients. A price that is computed server-side and served to Angular and React Native alike is a price that is consistent, auditable and changeable without shipping an app release, which matters when the same figure informs financing terms and a customer's decision to buy.\n\nIt also has to degrade gracefully. Inference is slower and less predictable than a database read, so valuation is best treated as its own service boundary with caching and sensible fallbacks, so that a delay in pricing one vehicle never takes the browsing and search experience down with it."
