        "body": "Supporting 1.2B+ JD in total transactions puts this squarely in fintech territory, where the tolerable error rate for money and inventory is zero. The hard cases are concurrent: two buyers committing to the same unique vehicle, a payment confirmation arriving twice, a financing application advancing while the underlying listing changes state.\n\nPostgreSQL is the reason those cases are tractable. ACID transactions let a reservation, a listing state change and a financial record commit or fail as one unit, and constraints enforced in the database hold even when a new code path forgets to check them. The database, not application convention, becomes the last line of defence.\n\nNestJS provides the surrounding discipline. Explicit service boundaries, injected dependencies and typed contracts keep transactional logic in one testable place, and make idempotent handling of repeated external callbacks a property of the module rather than a check someone remembered to add."
